{"title":"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Based_on_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Based on Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A cylindrical tank with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet is lying on its side. The tank is filled with water to a depth of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet. What is the volume of water, in cubic feet?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a62b57c568cffc0fb93acec0563804defc7d308.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 24\\pi - 36 \\sqrt {2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 24\\pi - 24 \\sqrt {3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 36\\pi - 36 \\sqrt {3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 36\\pi - 24 \\sqrt {2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 48\\pi - 36 \\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"766\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Based_on_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Based_on_Solution_1)\">Video Solution(Based on Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Based on Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I9RRrumPRK4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I9RRrumPRK4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Any vertical cross-section of the tank parallel with its base looks as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a702ddd98af1b8d46b21db963afe5d1ae0d985.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.8cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair s=(0,0), bottom=(0,-4), mid=(0,-2); pair x[]=intersectionpoints( (-10,-2)--(10,-2), circle(s,4) ); fill( arc(s,x[0],x[1]) -- cycle, lightgray ); draw( circle(s,4) ); dot(s); draw( s -- bottom ); label( &quot;$2$&quot;, (mid+bottom)/2, E ); draw ( s -- x[0] -- x[1] -- s ); label( &quot;$4$&quot;, (s+x[0])/2, NW ); label( &quot;$4$&quot;, (s+x[1])/2, NE ); label( &quot;$A$&quot;, s, N ); label( &quot;$B$&quot;, x[0], W ); label( &quot;$C$&quot;, x[1], E ); label( &quot;$D$&quot;, mid, NW ); label( &quot;$E$&quot;, bottom, S ); [/asy]\" width=\"312\" height=\"328\" />\n</p><p>The volume of water can be computed as the height of the tank times the area of the shaded part.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the size of the smaller angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6250647b3666c03d1363b3a401f37c1d9db3c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. We then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bda1e0012223e45a8f715966f79cbd65f93944a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{AD}{AC}=\\frac 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"129\" height=\"38\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d25be641607d3ca0d4632143cd3507a0c384b16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=60^\\circ$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The figure is symmetrical, so the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b39e026037707282c95dfdbfd6dc64c855a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a3b3a6ac9ce35e81e994a4bb0262344d345d2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />. Hence the shaded part consists of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8abd5f84144827235aa7c1926fdd1090ce59c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{120^\\circ}{360^\\circ} = \\frac 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" /> of the circle, minus the area of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> we can compute that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/2795ab70cffa329497c67a1f5424b8231218d4fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=\\sqrt{AC^2-AD^2}=\\sqrt{16-4}=2\\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"310\" height=\"19\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c39ac0f06b9847b380a95b581e394034ea2ebd5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4\\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />, and the area of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f67850bb5cd690dc2f5ac506731154d45854e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {2 \\cdot 4\\sqrt 3} 2 = 4\\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"117\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>The area of the shaded part is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/017ee37972b97e3452c3a06c13940f9088d6a575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4^2\\pi}3 - 4\\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"39\" />, and the volume of water is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e582fa2dca848a8b34fb98eb82fac713a7255b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\cdot\\left(\\frac{4^2\\pi}3 - 4\\sqrt 3\\right) = \\boxed{48\\pi - 36\\sqrt 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"265\" height=\"43\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a5bb2aa78132b4b716cfde4a9136c884d94c753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{E}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>Alternatively, we can solve for the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b7e5ec2db31e9aded4bb09881b42d1c439fce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, as it is congruent to a 30-60-90 triangle by the SSS congruency theorem. ~Williamgolly\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B\">2008 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\n